  "question": "Design a voting management system:\nVoter Management: Each individual can be a legitimate voter or an invalid voter. Each legitimate voter must register their voting area (i.e., district) through the system. Each legitimate voter can only register in one district.\nDistrict Management: The district to which a voter belongs is determined by their residential address. An address can be a town or a city. Some districts may include multiple towns; whereas some larger cities may also contain multiple districts.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0513\nCREATE TABLE `district` (\n  `district_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `district_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `district_type` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `parent_address_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`district_id`),\n  KEY `district_ibfk_1` (`parent_address_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `district_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_address_id`) REFERENCES `address` (`address_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `address` (\n  `address_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `address_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address_type` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `district_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`address_id`),\n  KEY `address_ibfk_1` (`district_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `address_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`district_id`) REFERENCES `district` (`district_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `voter` (\n  `voter_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `full_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `is_legitimate` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `residential_address_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `registered_district_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`voter_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `voter_ibfk_1` (`registered_district_id`),\n  KEY `voter_ibfk_2` (`residential_address_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `voter_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`registered_district_id`) REFERENCES `district` (`district_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `voter_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`residential_address_id`) REFERENCES `address` (`address_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
